# Frontend (Next.js) Rules

Applies to everything under `web/`.

- The POS screen is a plain online web page: it calls the backend API directly over
  HTTPS, with no offline persistence, local database, or sync queue (this was decided
  explicitly — see spec/00-overview.md). The only resilience expected is a short
  client-side retry (a few seconds, a couple of attempts) on a failed request before
  surfacing a clear error to the cashier. Do not add IndexedDB, service workers, or any
  offline-first machinery.
- Keyboard-first UX for POS: every action a cashier needs during a sale (add item by
  barcode, add serial, apply payment method, hold cart, finalize) must be reachable via
  keyboard shortcut, not just mouse click. Define shortcuts in one shared constants file,
  not scattered inline, so they stay consistent and documented.
- Branches are optional throughout the UI: never assume a branch selector is required.
  If the business has zero branches configured, all branch-scoped screens must still
  function (treating the whole business as one implicit location).
- Data fetching: use a single typed API client layer (e.g., generated from an OpenAPI
  spec, or a thin typed wrapper) — no raw `fetch` calls with inline URL strings scattered
  across components. Centralize base URL and auth header injection in one place.
- Forms: validate on the client for UX, but never trust client validation alone — assume
  the backend re-validates everything (this is a backend rule too, cross-reference
  00-global.mdc).
- No hardcoded currency symbols, VAT rates, or price formatting rules in components —
  pull from a shared formatting utility configured from backend-provided settings.
- Testing: component tests for anything with real interaction logic (the POS cart, the
  RMA status stepper, serial lookup). Don't bother testing pure presentational
  components with no logic — spend the effort where it matters.
